WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.610
Angle problems are solved by chains.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.450
You know one angle, a fact gives you the next,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.450
another fact gives the one after.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.080
The facts are few: a straight line makes one hundred and

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.785
eighty degrees, a full turn makes three hundred and

00:00:13.785 --> 00:00:17.300
sixty, and angles opposite each other where two lines

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.550
cross are equal.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.050
Competition diagrams may not be drawn to scale.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.820
Use the stated facts, a link at a time, and say which

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.890
angle rule justifies each link.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.320
Two parallel lines are crossed by a third line.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.100
One angle at the top is sixty-five degrees.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.300
Find the marked angle at the bottom.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.970
Pause and trace how the top crossing relates to

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:39.680
the bottom one.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.100
Because the lines are parallel, the top crossing is an

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.830
exact copy of the bottom one.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.690
Slide it down and it fits.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.020
So the angle in the matching position at the bottom is

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.570
also sixty-five degrees.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.050
These are called corresponding angles.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.860
The angle we want sits next to that sixty-five on

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:02.630
a straight line.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.310
Together they make one hundred and eighty.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.430
So the marked angle is one hundred and fifteen degrees.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.250
Two facts, two links, and the chain is complete.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.370
The same parallel-line fact proves something famous.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.550
Draw a line through the top of a triangle,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:19.970
parallel to the base.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.280
The two base angles reappear beside the top angle,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.930
and the three sit together on a straight line.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.080
So the angles in any triangle add up to one hundred

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:30.130
and eighty degrees.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.420
Add one more link for equal sides.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.930
In a triangle with two equal sides, the angles opposite

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.840
them are equal.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.510
If the top angle is forty, the other two share one

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.220
hundred and forty equally: seventy each.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.140
Build a chain.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.920
Name the fact for each link.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.520
Notebook challenge: a triangle has two equal sides,

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.820
and one of its two equal angles is fifty-five degrees.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:56.560
What is the third angle?
